 ```
 
+To list the built-in rules (for example, in an editor integration), the
+`getRules` method can be used:
+
+```javascript
+/**
+ * Gets information about the built-in rules.
+ *
+ * @returns {RuleInfo[]} One (new) object per built-in rule, in rule order.
+ */
+function getRules() { ... }
+```
+
+Each object has the rule's `names` and `tags` (arrays of strings), its
+`description`, its documentation URL as the string `information`, and whether
+it can fix what it reports as the boolean `fixable`. Every call returns new
+objects, so changing them does not affect `markdownlint`:
+
+```javascript
+import { getRules } from "markdownlint";
+
+// Displays the names of the fixable rules
+console.log(getRules().filter((rule) => rule.fixable).map((rule) => rule.names[0]));
+```
+
 [semver]: https://semver.org
 
